-- Named rejection: a regulative (deontic) rule has no relational image.
--
-- A Horn clause says what HOLDS; it has no vocabulary for what a party MUST do,
-- by when, or what happens when they do not. Collapsing an obligation to the
-- boolean "the obligation is in force" is precisely the loss the relational
-- middle-end refuses to make silently, so this is a batch LowerError with the
-- constructor-keyed kind LEDeontic rather than a fidelity note.

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Alice, Bob

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
  smoke

@export
`no smoking` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  SHANT smoke
  WITHIN 30
